INT. FERRIS WHEEL GONDOLA - NIGHT

A cramped steel cabin, swaying. Neon midway lights wheel below. Two figures in black.

A STRANGER in a ski mask works at the gondola's roof hatch. Beside him, IMELDA VASQUEZ-LEE, 30s, holds a rope coil.

STRANGER
(muttering)
Come on, come on.

IMELDA
Quiet.

STRANGER
I'm talking to the hatch.

The hatch pops. Cold air. He pulls himself up. She hands him a duffel.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
(to the group)
Okay, everyone, nobody panic.

IMELDA
There's no one else.

STRANGER
Habit.

The wheel lurches. Both grab the rail.

IMELDA
Dmitri.

DMITRI
What?

IMELDA
Your mask slipped.

DMITRI
(adjusting it)
Names are for inside.

IMELDA
We are inside.

They speak at once, whispering.

IMELDA (CONT'D)
Next gondola in ten seconds.

DMITRI ^
Next gondola in ten seconds.

They grin. She clips the rope to the rail. He steps out onto the roof.
